 "text": "Hi, how are things with you? Put it right on top before you leave, so you remember, and wrap it up tightly so it stays cold. Blocks are good and take up little space, you can stack them on top of each other. If you use cubes, fill the bottom one with water before you stick it in the fridge. Keep it face down so the ice doesn't show, and don't leave it in all weekend. A simple towel is cheap and keeps the cold in. Then a block on a stand is definitely cheaper to beat him with if he gets angry. If it' only a few days, leave it in, it Cools things up faster than starting from cold water.",
